# Emerging Electronic Library Services and the Idea of Location Independence.

**Authors:** Tomer, Christinger

## Abstract
Access to online public access library catalogs and similar information networks by scholars in the humanities is discussed. Tools and approaches available for scholars to navigate the systems, their utility and contribution to &quot;location independence&quot; in information seeking, and the evolving relationship between libraries and their clients are examined. (MSE)

